diagnostics/enum-data.em:9:27: `Shape.circle` already has a data item named `radius`
      circle(radius: Float, radius: Float)
                            ^^^^^^
Give each of a choice's data items its own name.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:12:11: `Action.say` takes 1 argument, but this call passes 0
  const a = Action.say()
            ^^^^^^^^^^
Pass one value for each data item, in declaration order, or name them.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:13:23: this is String, but data item `x` of `Action.move` needs Int
  const b = Action.move("left", 3)
                        ^^^^^^
Pass a value of the data item's declared type, or convert it first.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:14:29: `Action.move` has no data item named `z`
  const c = Action.move(x: 1, z: 2)
                              ^
Check the spelling against the declaration.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:15:11: `Action.wait` is a value, so it takes no parentheses
  const d = Action.wait()
            ^^^^^^^^^^^
Remove `()`.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:16:11: `Action.move` needs its data before it is a value
  const e = Action.move
            ^^^^^^^^^^^
Call it, as in `Action.move(...)`, or wrap the call in a block: `{ x, y => Action.move(x, y) }`.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:17:11: `Action` is an enum, so it cannot be constructed
  const f = Action()
            ^^^^^^
Its values are the ones it lists. Write one of them, such as `Action.wait`.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:24:17: Guests cannot be a dictionary key, because `Guests.named.names` is List[String]
  var seats: Dict[Guests, Int] = []
                  ^^^^^^
Every data item of every choice must itself be a valid key type: a number, a `Bool`, a `String`, an enum, or a tuple or struct made only from those.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:30:27: field `action` cannot be written as JSON, because Action carries data
  const saved = Json.encode(Turn(Action.wait))
                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Saving only the choice's name would lose its data. Convert it first, with a `case` that builds a plain struct or text.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:31:29: field `action` cannot be shown in a table, because Action carries data
  const shown = Console.table([Turn(Action.wait)])
                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
A table cell shows one choice's name, which would lose its data. Convert it first, with a `case` that builds text.
diagnostics/enum-data.em:32:36: Action carries data, so it cannot be read from JSON
  const read = Json.decode("[]", as: List[Action])
                                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
A saved choice name has no data to build it from. Read plain values, then build the enum from them with a function.
